1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,034
Once you know the game, try this.

2
00:00:02,354 --> 00:00:03,655
It's called a variant.

3
00:00:03,975 --> 00:00:06,216
A variant is a different way to play.

4
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:09,686
Turn every player board to its grey side.

5
00:00:10,006 --> 00:00:12,033
Everyone must use the same side.

6
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:16,333
On the grey side, the wall spaces have no colours.

7
00:00:17,466 --> 00:00:20,645
When a line is complete, you choose where its tile goes.

8
00:00:20,965 --> 00:00:22,735
Any empty space in that row.

9
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:26,959
But each colour may appear only once in each column.

10
00:00:27,279 --> 00:00:29,114
Blue is already in column three.

11
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:33,774
So Ana's blue tile may go in four spaces of row one.

12
00:00:35,683 --> 00:00:37,112
She picks the left one.

13
00:00:37,432 --> 00:00:39,693
It scores like normal: two points.

14
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,658
Each row still holds each colour only once, too.

15
00:00:44,466 --> 00:00:45,874
Now look at line two.

16
00:00:46,194 --> 00:00:47,645
It's complete, with red.

17
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:50,397
But red is already in both free columns.

18
00:00:52,383 --> 00:00:55,156
So all tiles of that line fall to the floor line.

19
00:00:56,266 --> 00:01:01,322
Everything else is the same: scoring, the floor line, the end and the bonuses.

20
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:03,329
Remember.

21
00:01:03,649 --> 00:01:07,019
On the grey side, you choose any empty space in the row.

22
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,582
Each colour appears once per row and once per column.

23
00:01:10,902 --> 00:01:14,657
If no space is allowed, the whole line goes to the floor line.

24
00:01:14,977 --> 00:01:16,790
Next: watch a whole game.
